<article class="env-lemma" id="083R">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/083R">Lemma <span data-tag="083R">67.40.2</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$. The following are equivalent </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$f$ is proper, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
for every scheme $Z$ and every morphism $Z \to Y$ the projection $Z \times _ Y X \to Z$ is proper, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
for every affine scheme $Z$ and every morphism $Z \to Y$ the projection $Z \times _ Y X \to Z$ is proper, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
there exists a scheme $V$ and a surjective étale morphism $V \to Y$ such that $V \times _ Y X \to V$ is proper, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
there exists a Zariski covering $Y = \bigcup Y_ i$ such that each of the morphisms $f^{-1}(Y_ i) \to Y_ i$ is proper. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Combine Lemmas <a href="/tag/03KM" data-tag="03KM">67.4.12</a>, <a href="/tag/040Y" data-tag="040Y">67.23.4</a>, <a href="/tag/03KG" data-tag="03KG">67.8.8</a>, and <a href="/tag/03IT" data-tag="03IT">67.9.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>